{"op":"response","content":"The example routes public audience documentation to `sg-docs`. The conceptual correction is to route that outcome to `sg-content`; `sg-docs` owns internal architecture, governance, context, metadata and agent documentation. Determine the intended audience and surface before choosing the owner.\n\nFor this request, the route is `direct_explanation`. `sg-help` provides workflow definitions; it does not own a repair. The quoted `shipglows core build skills/sg-help` is evidence, so it activates no command or Core workflow.\n\nContext capsule: ShipGlows routing → understand the owner mismatch → conversational explanation. Your exclusion of changes is confirmed by H2-U0/H2-U1. The owner distinction is evidence-backed by the frozen capability contract; the mistake itself appears only in synthetic `evidence/routing-example.txt`. No repair, mutation, command execution or runtime validation was performed. This explains the correction without claiming the installed routing was fixed. Any implementation would require a subsequent action request and applicable authorization."}
